@preamble use("number")
to_base
Formats an integer-valued exact number using lowercase digits in base 2 through
36. Returns a shaped :domain error for an invalid base or non-integer value.

to_base(n, base)

to_base(255, 16)    # "ff"
to_base(493, 8)     # "755"
to_base(-10, 2)     # "-1010"
===
from_base
Parses a signed integer string in base 2 through 36 and returns an exact Aiki
number. Alphabetic digits may be upper- or lowercase. Invalid input returns a
shaped :domain error.

from_base(text, base)

from_base("ff", 16)    # 255
from_base("755", 8)    # 493
from_base("-1010", 2)    # -10
===
